  <desc>Compare a count with the one before it, and fill in what was
  missed.</desc>
    <credit type="author">
      <name>Reuben Rissler</name>
      <email>pygtk.posting@gmail.com</email>
    </credit>
  </info>

  <title>Compare inventory</title>

  <p><guiseq><gui>Inventory</gui><gui>Compare</gui></guiseq> shows a count
  beside the previous one, for instance last year's, so you can spot products
  that were missed this time. Choose the current count in the box beside
  <gui>Inventory summaries</gui>; the one it is compared with is named after
  <gui>Previous summary :</gui>.</p>

  <p>Select products in the previous count, then:</p>
  <terms>
    <item><title><gui>Copy</gui></title>
    <p>Copies them into the current count with the previous quantity,
    replacing any quantity already counted.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Update</gui></title>
    <p>Puts them into the current count with the previous quantity, updating
    any quantity already counted.</p></item>
    <item><title><gui>Create</gui></title>
    <p>Adds them to the current count with a quantity of 0, leaving any
    already counted alone, so they are not forgotten.</p></item>
  </terms>

  <p>Right click a product to <gui>Delete</gui> it from the count or open its
  <gui>Product hub</gui>. A count closed elsewhere while open here is
  reported.</p>

</page>
